Exact-output integer Taylor evaluation for the count exponential helpers
======================================================================

The original count code evaluates S48(x)=sum_{i=0}^{48}x^i/i!, then rounds
down for exp_lower. For exp_upper it adds the same geometric tail
x^49/49!/(1-x/50) and rounds up. The scale is10^12. No term or bound changes.

For x=a/b>=0, b>0, let c_i=48!/i!, an integer. The polynomial numerator
N=sum_{i=0}^{48}c_i*a^i*b^(48-i) has denominator D=48!*b^48.
The code starts from c48=1 and applies integer Horner arithmetic while
updating the power of b. Induction gives exactly N and D without reducing
the intermediate fractions. Consequently floor(10^12*N/D)/10^12 is exactly
the original exp_lower output.

The unchanged tail is50*a^49/[49!*b^48*(50*b-a)]. The exact combined
numerator and denominator of S48+tail are therefore
 N*[49*(50*b-a)]+50*a^49,    D*[49*(50*b-a)].
Their upward integer division at the same scale gives exactly exp_upper.
The denominator is positive for x<50. The original scope x<10 is retained
unless the caller explicitly selects the separately reviewed generalized
x<50 scope. No upper exponential is evaluated at or above50.

The named installer requires Fraction arithmetic, the existing scale, and
one common original helper pair in the two active count modules. Its typed
bounded caches affect only evaluation order. Inputs are Fraction or literal
int; bool/float and arbitrary arithmetic objects are rejected. All current
exact count calls supply Fractions. Neither helper reads a mutable profile,
target, support radius, n or moment cap. Their mathematical outputs are
unchanged, not merely outward relaxations.

Use only in a newly named count package. Bind this source/proof, the copied
original kernel and whole-cell equivalence results. Active/completed count
sources must remain frozen; existing receipt hashes cannot be relabeled as
acceptance under this new runtime. A full count acceptance still freshly
evaluates every leaf.
